// ============================================================================
// Detection: Client Certificate Credential via CSR (Self-Approved)
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1098 - Account Manipulation
// Source: AKSAuditAdmin
// ============================================================================

// HOW THIS DETECTION WORKS
// -------------------------
// Kubernetes lets you request a signed client certificate through the
// CertificateSigningRequest (CSR) API: you `create` a CSR, then someone with
// rights `update`s its /approval subresource, and the cluster CA signs it. A
// signed client cert authenticates to the API server as whatever user/groups
// the CSR named — so a self-approved CSR is a way to MINT durable credentials
// (T1098 Account Manipulation / credential creation).
//
// The strong signal here is a SEPARATION-OF-DUTY violation: the SAME principal
// both creates the CSR and approves it. Legitimate flows split requester from
// approver (kubelet requests, certificate-controller approves).
//
// TABLE: AKSAuditAdmin — the "admin" slice of the Kubernetes audit log. It keeps
//        WRITE/mutating events (create/update/delete) but not routine reads, so
//        it is the right, cheaper table for approval-workflow tampering.

AKSAuditAdmin
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)                                       // prune to the recent window first
| where ObjectRef.resource == "certificatesigningrequests"           // only CSR API objects
// Keep BOTH halves of the flow: the initial create, AND updates that hit the
// /approval subresource (the moment a CSR is signed off). Either alone is noise;
// the pair from one user is the finding.
| where (Verb == "create") or (Verb == "update" and ObjectRef.subresource == "approval")
// Tune: kubelets create CSRs and certificate-controller approves them — both system:*.
| where User.username !startswith "system:"                          // drop built-in control-plane actors
| project TimeGenerated, User = tostring(User.username), Verb,       // project = keep just these columns...
          Sub = tostring(ObjectRef.subresource), CSR = tostring(ObjectRef.name), RequestUri
| sort by TimeGenerated asc   // create then approval from one user = self-signed credential
| extend MitreTechnique = "T1098"    // tag hits with the ATT&CK technique
